{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getfacetedrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type getFacetedRowModel = () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":" function to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.facetedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":". A default implementation is provided via the exported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model with all other column filters applied, excluding its own filter. Useful for displaying faceted result counts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getfaceteduniquevalues","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedUniqueValues"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getFacetedUniqueValues: () => Map<any, number>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedUniqueValues"},{"type":"text","value":" function to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.getFacetedUniqueValues"},{"type":"text","value":". A default implementation is provided via the exported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedUniqueValues"},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"computes and returns"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Map"},{"type":"text","value":" of unique values and their occurrences derived from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getFacetedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":". Useful for displaying faceted result values."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getfacetedminmaxvalues","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedMinMaxValues"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getFacetedMinMaxValues: () => Map<any, number>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedMinMaxValues"},{"type":"text","value":" function to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.getFacetedMinMaxValues"},{"type":"text","value":". A default implementation is provided via the exported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFacetedMinMaxValues"},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"computes and returns"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a min/max tuple derived from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getFacetedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":". Useful for displaying faceted result values."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcolumnfacetedrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getColumnFacetedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getColumnFacetedRowModel: (columnId: string) => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the faceted row model for a given columnId."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"column-api","text":"Column API","level":2},{"id":"getfacetedrowmodel","text":"getFacetedRowModel","level":3},{"id":"getfaceteduniquevalues","text":"getFacetedUniqueValues","level":3},{"id":"getfacetedminmaxvalues","text":"getFacetedMinMaxValues","level":3},{"id":"table-options","text":"Table Options","level":2},{"id":"getcolumnfacetedrowmodel","text":"getColumnFacetedRowModel","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Column API\n\n### `getFacetedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ntype getFacetedRowModel = () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\n> ⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid `getFacetedRowModel` function to `options.facetedRowModel`. A default implementation is provided via the exported `getFacetedRowModel` function.\n\nReturns the row model with all other column filters applied, excluding its own filter. Useful for displaying faceted result counts.\n\n### `getFacetedUniqueValues`\n\n```tsx\ngetFacetedUniqueValues: () => Map<any, number>\n```\n\n> ⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid `getFacetedUniqueValues` function to `options.getFacetedUniqueValues`. A default implementation is provided via the exported `getFacetedUniqueValues` function.\n\nA function that **computes and returns** a `Map` of unique values and their occurrences derived from `column.getFacetedRowModel`. Useful for displaying faceted result values.\n\n### `getFacetedMinMaxValues`\n\n```tsx\ngetFacetedMinMaxValues: () => Map<any, number>\n```\n\n> ⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid `getFacetedMinMaxValues` function to `options.getFacetedMinMaxValues`. A default implementation is provided via the exported `getFacetedMinMaxValues` function.\n\nA function that **computes and returns** a min/max tuple derived from `column.getFacetedRowModel`. Useful for displaying faceted result values.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `getColumnFacetedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetColumnFacetedRowModel: (columnId: string) => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the faceted row model for a given columnId.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Column Faceting APIs\nid: column-faceting\n---\n\n## Column API\n\n### `getFacetedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ntype getFacetedRowModel = () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\n> ⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid `getFacetedRowModel` function to `options.facetedRowModel`. A default implementation is provided via the exported `getFacetedRowModel` function.\n\nReturns the row model with all other column filters applied, excluding its own filter. Useful for displaying faceted result counts.\n\n### `getFacetedUniqueValues`\n\n```tsx\ngetFacetedUniqueValues: () => Map<any, number>\n```\n\n> ⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid `getFacetedUniqueValues` function to `options.getFacetedUniqueValues`. A default implementation is provided via the exported `getFacetedUniqueValues` function.\n\nA function that **computes and returns** a `Map` of unique values and their occurrences derived from `column.getFacetedRowModel`. Useful for displaying faceted result values.\n\n### `getFacetedMinMaxValues`\n\n```tsx\ngetFacetedMinMaxValues: () => Map<any, number>\n```\n\n> ⚠️ Requires that you pass a valid `getFacetedMinMaxValues` function to `options.getFacetedMinMaxValues`. A default implementation is provided via the exported `getFacetedMinMaxValues` function.\n\nA function that **computes and returns** a min/max tuple derived from `column.getFacetedRowModel`. Useful for displaying faceted result values.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `getColumnFacetedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetColumnFacetedRowModel: (columnId: string) => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the faceted row model for a given columnId.\n"}
